<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE lm2d-jiuquan ascent</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Long March 2D Y108 / Origins Pathfinder A-D (Jiuquan LA-94, SLS-2 / 603) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
FLOWN 2026-11-11T11:41:00Z (19:41 BJT; Xinhua http://www.xinhuanet.com/20261111/f62e737993404c6aa3ba9246a6118598/c.html; CSSAR http://www.cssar.cas.cn/xwdt2015/xwsd2015/202611/t20261111_8307991.html; LL2 Success): LM-2D Y108, Origins (TanYuan) Pathfinder A-D, Long March flight 677. RETIMED +60 s from LL2 NET 11:40Z.
Event times: SAST TYPICAL LM-2D sequence via https://sat.huijiwiki.com/wiki/长征二号丁: pitch-over 17.0 s, S1 cutoff 153.9 s, sep 155.1 s, fairing 185.1 s, S2 main cutoff 324.1 s, S2 vernier cutoff 705.1 s (payload sep 737.1 s not in this file).
Azimuth 192.23 deg: great-circle bearing from pad to centroid 35.554N 98.863E (614 km) of NOTAM ZLHW A5728/26 danger area (valid 2026-11-11 11:32-12:05Z; https://space-notices.com/notice/notam-ZLHW-A5728%2F26), INFERRED stage-1 impact zone.
Orbit: 600 km dawn-dusk sun-synchronous per CSSAR (retuned 2026-11-11 from the earlier ASSUMED 500 km); circular insertion at vernier cutoff ASSUMED.
Altitude knots (t s: km; times published typical sequence, ALTITUDES ASSUMED = this board&#x27;s 3DOF sim at those times, final = published orbit): 0:0, 17:0.3, 153.9:63.6, 155.1:64.9, 185.1:97.1, 324.1:262.3, 705.1:600
Horizontal ground speed ASSUMED linear 0 -&gt; 7.632 km/s (circular v at 600 km minus Earth rotation along Az) at T+705.1 s. File ends at final cutoff.
Pad (LL2): 40.960482N 100.298059E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s.
Constant-azimuth rhumb Az=192.23 deg from pad. Velocity ECEF: v_horiz along Az + hdot Up in local ENU.
T0 used: 2026-11-11T11:41:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.</description>
